var t=[{slug:"how-to-find-right-rishta-pakistan",title:"How to Find the Right Match in Pakistan \u2014 A Complete Guide",excerpt:"Practical steps for families and individuals searching for a halal, compatible marriage partner across Pakistan and overseas.",category:"Match Guide",author:"Hum Rishta Team",readMinutes:8,publishedAt:"2026-06-15",coverGradient:"linear-gradient(135deg, #6B0F1A 0%, #9B1B30 50%, #C9A227 100%)",coverIcon:"\u{1F48D}",metaDescription:"Learn how to find the right match in Pakistan with family involvement, profile tips, and halal matrimonial best practices.",content:["Finding the right match is one of the most important decisions in life. In Pakistan, this journey is deeply connected to family values, faith, and cultural traditions. Whether you are in Karachi, Lahore, Islamabad, or living overseas, a thoughtful approach saves time and brings blessing to the process.","Start by discussing expectations openly with your family. Age range, education, city, sect, and lifestyle preferences should be clear before you begin searching. When everyone understands the goals, mismatched proposals are reduced and conversations stay respectful.","A complete matrimonial profile makes a strong first impression. Share accurate details about education, profession, family background, and what you are looking for in a partner. Honesty builds trust \u2014 the foundation of every successful marriage.","Use filters wisely on Hum Rishta: search by province, city, religion, marital status, and education. Review profiles carefully and note compatibility in values, not just appearance or income.","When you find a promising profile, request contact through the platform. Admin verification helps protect both parties. Meet families in a respectful setting, involve elders, and ask meaningful questions about faith, finances, and future plans.","Remember: patience and prayer are part of the journey. The right match comes at the right time. May Allah make your search easy and blessed."]},{slug:"questions-before-marriage-pakistani-couples",title:"10 Important Questions to Ask Before Marriage in Pakistani Culture",excerpt:"Essential questions about faith, family, finances, and lifestyle that every couple and family should discuss before nikah.",category:"Marriage Tips",author:"Hum Rishta Team",readMinutes:7,publishedAt:"2026-06-08",coverGradient:"linear-gradient(135deg, #4a1942 0%, #9B1B30 60%, #D4567A 100%)",coverIcon:"\u{1F4AC}",metaDescription:"Ten essential pre-marriage questions for Pakistani couples and families \u2014 faith, finances, family, and lifestyle compatibility.",content:["Before nikah, meaningful conversation prevents misunderstandings later. These questions are not meant to create doubt \u2014 they help both families align expectations with honesty and respect.","1. Religious practice: How do you practice Islam daily? What are your expectations about prayer, fasting, and raising children with Islamic values?","2. Family involvement: What role will parents and in-laws play after marriage? How will decisions be made together?","3. Finances: Who will manage household expenses? Are there debts, savings goals, or support obligations for parents or siblings?","4. Living arrangements: Will you live independently or with family? What are your views on joint family living?","5. Career and education: Do you support your spouse working or studying after marriage? Any relocation plans?","6. Children: When do you hope to have children? How many? What parenting style and values matter most?","7. Health and lifestyle: Any medical conditions families should know about? Views on diet, social life, and travel?","8. Conflict resolution: How do you handle disagreements? What does respect look like during difficult conversations?","9. Boundaries with others: Views on privacy, social media, and friendships after marriage.","10. Long-term vision: Where do you see yourselves in five to ten years \u2014 city, career, family goals?","Discuss these topics calmly with family present when appropriate. A marriage built on clarity is stronger than one built on assumptions."]},{slug:"online-matrimonial-safety-tips",title:"Online Matrimonial Safety Tips \u2014 Protect Yourself on Matchmaking Platforms",excerpt:"Stay safe while searching for marriage online: verify profiles, protect personal data, and recognize red flags.",category:"Safety",author:"Hum Rishta Team",readMinutes:6,publishedAt:"2026-05-28",coverGradient:"linear-gradient(135deg, #1e3a5f 0%, #9B1B30 70%, #C4314E 100%)",coverIcon:"\u{1F6E1}\uFE0F",metaDescription:"Online matrimonial safety tips for Pakistan \u2014 verify profiles, avoid scams, protect personal information on matchmaking websites.",content:["Online matchmaking platforms make it easier to connect across cities and countries, but safety must come first. Follow these guidelines to protect yourself and your family.","Never share CNIC copies, bank details, or passwords with strangers. Legitimate platforms like Hum Rishta use admin-verified contact requests instead of exposing numbers publicly.","Be cautious of anyone who pressures you to decide quickly, asks for money, or refuses family involvement. These are common warning signs in matrimonial scams.","Verify information independently. Cross-check education, profession, and family details during family meetings. Trust is earned through consistency over time.","Meet in safe, public or family settings for initial interactions. Avoid isolated meetings with unknown individuals.","Report suspicious profiles or harassment through the platform complaint system. Admin review helps keep the community safe for everyone.","Use strong passwords and log out on shared devices. Your matrimonial account contains personal information that deserves protection."]},{slug:"complete-matrimonial-profile-tips",title:"How to Create a Complete Matrimonial Profile That Gets Responses",excerpt:"Profile photo, about me, partner preferences, and contact details \u2014 everything you need for a trustworthy matrimonial profile.",category:"Profile Tips",author:"Hum Rishta Team",readMinutes:5,publishedAt:"2026-05-20",coverGradient:"linear-gradient(135deg, #2d5016 0%, #9B1B30 50%, #C9A227 100%)",coverIcon:"\u{1F4DD}",metaDescription:"Tips to create a complete matrimonial profile on Hum Rishta \u2014 photos, about me, preferences, and verification for better matches.",content:["Your profile is your introduction to hundreds of families. A complete, honest profile receives more serious inquiries than an empty or vague one.","Upload a clear, recent photo with a modest, respectful presentation. Profiles with photos receive significantly more views, but never use heavily filtered or misleading images.",'Write a genuine "About Me" section. Mention your education, profession, values, hobbies, and what makes you unique. Avoid generic phrases \u2014 specificity attracts compatible matches.',"Fill partner preferences honestly: age range, city, education, marital status, and any important requirements. Realistic preferences lead to better matches.","Add verified contact numbers through the platform. WhatsApp and phone options help families connect after admin-approved requests.","Keep your profile updated. Marital status, city, or profession changes should be reflected promptly so search results stay accurate.","Complete profiles also help admin verification during contact requests \u2014 speeding up approval when you find someone interesting."]},{slug:"family-role-pakistani-rishta-process",title:"The Role of Family in the Pakistani Matchmaking Process",excerpt:"Why family involvement matters, how to balance tradition with personal choice, and tips for respectful family meetings.",category:"Culture",author:"Hum Rishta Team",readMinutes:6,publishedAt:"2026-05-12",coverGradient:"linear-gradient(135deg, #5c3d1e 0%, #9B1B30 55%, #E8A0BF 100%)",coverIcon:"\u{1F468}\u200D\u{1F469}\u200D\u{1F467}\u200D\u{1F466}",metaDescription:"Understanding family involvement in Pakistani matchmaking culture \u2014 traditions, meetings, and balancing personal choice with family guidance.",content:["In Pakistani culture, marriage is not only between two individuals \u2014 it connects two families. Understanding this helps navigate the matchmaking process with wisdom and respect.","Parents and elders often bring experience, network, and prayers to the search. Their involvement can filter incompatible matches and provide emotional support during a stressful time.","At the same time, the bride and groom should have a voice in the final decision. Islam emphasizes consent (ridha) from both parties. The ideal process combines family guidance with personal choice.","Family meetings work best when both sides prepare questions in advance, dress appropriately, and keep conversations focused on compatibility rather than material demands.","Avoid comparing multiple proposals disrespectfully or sharing private details from one meeting with another family. Confidentiality and good manners reflect your family's character.","When using online platforms, involve family early. Share profiles with parents before requesting contact. This transparency prevents misunderstandings and builds trust."]},{slug:"overseas-pakistanis-finding-rishta",title:"Guide for Overseas Pakistanis Finding a Match Back Home",excerpt:"How Pakistanis in UK, USA, UAE, and Canada can search for compatible matches in Pakistan with family support.",category:"Overseas",author:"Hum Rishta Team",readMinutes:7,publishedAt:"2026-05-01",coverGradient:"linear-gradient(135deg, #0f4c75 0%, #9B1B30 45%, #D4AF37 100%)",coverIcon:"\u2708\uFE0F",metaDescription:"Matchmaking guide for overseas Pakistanis \u2014 search profiles in Pakistan, involve family, and plan meetings for nikah across borders.",content:["Millions of Pakistanis live abroad while their hearts remain connected to home. Finding a match across borders has unique challenges \u2014 distance, time zones, and differing expectations.","Start by clarifying your long-term plan: Will your spouse relocate abroad? Will you settle in Pakistan? These answers narrow the search significantly.","Use Hum Rishta's overseas location options to register your current country while searching profiles in Pakistani cities. Families in both places can review matches together on video calls.","Involve a trusted family member in Pakistan who can attend meetings on your behalf when you cannot travel immediately. Video introductions are useful, but in-person family meetings remain important before commitment.","Discuss visa, financial, and cultural adjustment expectations openly. Overseas marriages succeed when both sides understand the practical realities of relocation or long-distance engagement periods.","Plan visits with enough time for multiple family meetings \u2014 not just one rushed trip. Blessing comes with patience and thoroughness.","May Allah unite overseas Pakistanis with righteous partners who share their values and dreams."]}];function n(e){return t.find(i=>i.slug===e)}function s(e,i=3){return t.filter(a=>a.slug!==e).slice(0,i)}export{t as a,n as b,s as c};
